    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale project in the Caribbean or Latin America**, the owner’s initial brand list usually centers on the following groups:\n\n### Core full-service shortlist\n\n| Brand family | Brands commonly considered | Typical fit |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | **Marriott Hotels, Westin, Sheraton, Renaissance, Le Méridien** | Large urban hotels, resorts, convention/group business |\n|  | **Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio** | Independent or locally distinctive hotels seeking distribution without rigid brand identity |\n| **Hilton** | **Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Curio Collection, Canopy, Tapestry Collection, Embassy Suites** | Hilton for conventional full service; Curio/Tapestry for conversions and lifestyle resorts; Canopy for urban lifestyle |\n| **Hyatt** | **Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric** | Regency for meetings and full-service resorts; Centric for lifestyle-oriented urban or leisure locations |\n|  | **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** | Distinctive resorts and historic or experiential properties, often positioned at the upper-upscale/luxury boundary |\n| **IHG** | **Hotel Indigo, Kimpton, Crowne Plaza, voco** | Indigo/Kimpton for lifestyle; Crowne Plaza for corporate and meetings; voco for flexible conversions |\n| **Accor** | **Pullman, Swissôtel, MGallery** | Pullman for business/group demand; Swissôtel for premium full service; MGallery for distinctive independent-style assets |\n| **Minor Hotels** | **NH Collection** | Particularly relevant in Spanish-speaking Latin American urban markets |\n| **Wyndham** | **Wyndham Grand, Wyndham Alltra** | Full-service resorts and all-inclusive projects |\n| **Radisson/Choice** | **Radisson Blu** | Select urban and resort markets where the system has meaningful regional distribution |\n\nSTR’s February 2026 classifications place brands such as Marriott, Westin, Sheraton, Renaissance, Le Méridien, Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio, Hilton, Curio, Canopy, Tapestry, Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric, Hotel Indigo, Kimpton, Pullman, Swissôtel, NH Collection, Wyndham Grand and Radisson Blu in the **upper-upscale chain scale**. Some frequently compared alternatives—such as Crowne Plaza, voco and DoubleTree—currently sit in the adjacent upscale category, while MGallery, InterContinental and several soft brands may fall into luxury. ([costar.com](https://www.costar.com/products/str-benchmark/resources/guidelines/str-chain-scales))\n\n### For a Caribbean all-inclusive resort\n\nThe shortlist usually changes to include:\n\n- **Hyatt Vivid**\n- **Dreams Resorts & Spas**\n- **Secrets Resorts & Spas** for adults-only positioning\n- **Hyatt Ziva or Hyatt Zilara** if the economics support luxury positioning\n- **Wyndham Alltra**\n- **Iberostar Selection**\n- **Meliá / Paradisus**\n- **Royal Hideaway**\n- **Royalton**\n- Selected **Marriott all-inclusive brands**, including Autograph Collection opportunities\n\nHyatt’s regional portfolio is especially broad because it includes traditional full-service, lifestyle and all-inclusive platforms. STR currently classifies Hyatt Vivid, Wyndham Alltra and Iberostar Selection as upper upscale, while Dreams, Secrets, Ziva, Zilara and Royalton generally compete in luxury. ([newsroom.hyatt.com](https://newsroom.hyatt.com/UnboundAnniversaryGrowth2026))\n\n### Practical “first-round” shortlist\n\nFor a conventional **200–350-key upper-upscale urban or resort hotel**, a representative first round would often be:\n\n1. **Marriott Hotels**\n2. **Westin**\n3. **Autograph Collection**\n4. **Hilton Hotels & Resorts**\n5. **Curio Collection**\n6. **Hyatt Regency**\n7. **Hotel Indigo or Kimpton**\n8. **Pullman**\n9. **NH Collection**\n10. **Wyndham Grand**\n\nFor a smaller, design-led, conversion or locally distinctive property, the likely emphasis shifts toward **Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio, Curio Collection, Tapestry Collection, The Unbound Collection, Hotel Indigo, Kimpton and MGallery**. Soft brands are particularly active in the region because they let owners retain more of the hotel’s identity and can be easier to apply to conversions. Hilton reported strong 2025 CALA signing activity for Curio and Tapestry, while IHG has identified soft brands, conversions and lifestyle hotels as major regional growth channels. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands/premium-brands))\n\nThe final shortlist should be narrowed by **destination, urban versus resort format, all-inclusive versus EP, room count, meeting space, branded residences, required key money, territorial availability, management versus franchise preference, and the brand’s existing market-area protection**.",
